<title>USA: McDonald's sets first &quot;Campaign 55&quot; item.</title>
<headline>McDonald's sets first &quot;Campaign 55&quot; item.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald's Corp said Wednesday its Big Mac sandwich will be the first of its menu items to be featured in its rotating &quot;Campaign 55&quot; promotion, which begins Friday.</p>
<p>As previously reported, McDonald's 21,000 U.S. restaurants will sell the Big Mac for 55 cents when customers also buy any size drink and any size french fries.</p>
<p>The company said its Quarter Pounder with Cheese will be the next sandwich featured in the promotion, starting in June.</p>
<p>McDonald's kicked off &quot;Campaign 55&quot; earlier this month with four different breakfast offers that will continue indefinitely, the company said.</p>
<p>McDonald's shares closed unchanged Wednesday at 51-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
